CASE = [
 Q("<b>Case study.</b> Hiware Bazar in Maharashtra once faced severe water shortage. Under its Sarpanch, Popatrao Pawar, villagers built structures to collect rainwater and planted trees. Over time the water table rose, farming improved and the village became prosperous. The Sarpanch received the Padma Shri. "
   "(i) Who was the Sarpanch of Hiware Bazar? (ii) Name one step taken to solve the water shortage. (iii) Name the body that is headed by a Sarpanch. (iv) What does this case show about the role of a village leader and villagers?",
   "(i) Popatrao Pawar (1). (ii) Rainwater harvesting or planting trees (1). (iii) Gram Panchayat (1). (iv) A committed leader can guide development (1); the change succeeded because villagers cooperated in following the decisions (1).", "1+1+1+2"),
 Q("<b>Case study.</b> A village panchayat in Uttar Pradesh holds a Gram Sabha meeting. The Sarpanch reads out the village accounts, and villagers ask questions about the repair of a school building. The Panchayat Secretary records the decisions in the register. "
   "(i) Who attends the Gram Sabha? (ii) Who is the head of the Gram Panchayat? (iii) Who keeps the records of meetings? (iv) Why is it important that villagers can question the Panchayat in the Gram Sabha?",
   "(i) All adult voters of the village (1). (ii) The Sarpanch (1). (iii) The Panchayat Secretary (1). (iv) It makes the Panchayat accountable to the people (1); villagers can raise local needs and check that money is used properly (1).", "1+1+1+2"),
 Q("<b>Case study.</b> Ramesh is a farmer. He wants a road from his village to the market. The Gram Panchayat sends the request to the Panchayat Samiti at the block level, which coordinates with the Zila Parishad at the district level. Together they get the road built under a rural road scheme. "
   "(i) Name the block-level body. (ii) Name the district-level body. (iii) Which tier did the request begin from? (iv) Why does Panchayati Raj have three tiers instead of one?",
   "(i) Panchayat Samiti (1). (ii) Zila Parishad (1). (iii) The village tier, the Gram Panchayat (1). (iv) Different matters affect a village, a block or a district (1); three tiers let work be shared and coordinated at the right level (1).", "1+1+1+2"),
]

